  "RIBS: the 24 shipped Z-Anatomy ribs lie a median 16.1 mm (Z->label) / 15.0 mm (label->Z) from her TotalSegmentator rib labels (Q168 fitted one similarity per side onto the old dilated bundle ribs): rib-cage width 12-30 mm too narrow (e.g. y 440: her 263 vs Z 228 mm; y 520: 235 vs 186), mid-thorax A-P depth 25-40 mm too deep (y 320: her 146 vs Z 185); lowest ribs ended 30 mm high (eighth left rib 33 mm off).",
  "LUMBAR SPINE: Z L3/L4/L5 sit 22-29 mm too high against her vertebra labels (7/10/13 mm median); T1-T12 are within 1-3 mm; pelvis, sternum, scapula, clavicle within 1.3-2.2 mm (not errors).",
  "SKIN: the 52 trunk skin patches sit a median 28 mm (p90 69 mm) inside her CT skin (front/back sectors: 21.8 / 44.8 mm); 7.4 % of their vertices lie outside her skin (gluteal 39 %, sacral 22 %), 2.2 % of faces flipped against the source normal; V-shaped pleats under both breasts, skin torn open at the lower chest in the side view.",
  "SOFT TISSUE: shares the Q168 per-bone blend: 10.6 % of trunk muscle vertices inside her lung label and 16.7 % inside an organ label (now 1.1 % / 5.3 %), cartilage 7.6 % inside organs (now 0.3 %); rectus abdominis 20.6 mm and diaphragm 12.5 mm from her own CT meshes; fascia/pectoral sheets pleated at the costal margin."
 ],
